# v4l2loopback, cross-compiled on the laptop against this repo's kernel with
# tools/c20e-build-v4l2loopback.sh. It exists because the C20e's ISP capture node
# is multiplanar V4L2, which Qt, PipeWire and libcamera all refuse; the loopback
# gives one ordinary single-planar camera device that applications accept.
#
# source    https://github.com/umlaeute/v4l2loopback.git @ v0.15.4
#           (0f9ee86760b7f2bea174b7e3e7a1d38845da0ab4)
# kernel    6.1.172
# vermagic  6.1.172 SMP mod_unload aarch64
# built     2026-09-23T03:36Z
#
# The module has no kernel ABI checks beyond vermagic (CONFIG_MODVERSIONS is off
# in this kernel), so it keeps loading across kernel rebuilds as long as
# UTS_RELEASE stays the same. Rebuild it if the kernel version changes.
